      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. I'll improve understandability by splitting the single dense method into focused per-variant test methods with descriptive names, and by using named constants to make each assertion's intent obvious.Now I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version splits the original monolithic `testRoundTrip` method into six focused, descriptively-named test methods (one per DOCTYPE variant), adds named constants for expected values, and uses Javadoc comments to explain the HTML-vs-XML behavioral difference being verified in each case — making the intent of every assertion immediately clear without changing any runtime behaviour."
